From ab24db87b1f58c8447b01ba62fae3bab9159452c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HampterDev <131729366+HampterDev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 18:14:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Skip skin-folder files without an extension

skin_mgr_scan lists the .\skin folder: folders become skins, .zip
files zip skins, and every other file is skipped. To find the
extension it passed str_find_last(fd.cFileName, '.') to
string_assign_cstr, and for a file without a '.' in its name
str_find_last returns NULL, so strlen(NULL) crashed the client at
startup.

Such a file is now skipped like any other file that is not a zip skin.

Validation: the new test_skin_scan runs the extracted skin_mgr_scan,
with str_find_last and text_to_lower, over a fake .\skin listing with
FindFirstFileA, FindNextFileA and FindClose stubbed: a folder, README,
LICENSE and a file named zip (no '.'), notes.txt, Blue.ZIP and
Night.zip must give the folder and the two zip skins with their paths
and the current skin, and a folder of only README no skins. The test
crashes with an access violation on the previous code. Release build
without warnings.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VaQB81YtRGLtH8zvfX7WTY
